@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Admission effects review
+
+v1 has a concrete source-level scope hazard: its simplified-AST demand can omit selected relative-unit syntax. v2 removes the collector from A and uses actual admitted substituted-token flags. This is not a confirmed browser bug or a settled normative cycle result. No eager URL fetch or global random-base evaluation was found in the inspected parse paths. Zoom readiness remains unresolved pending paired observations; no native acceptance is claimed.
+
+The reviewed v2 delta replaces semantic-or-selected classification with selected token flags. Its two cascade files are unchanged from v1. SCC ownership, whole-value grammar admission, taint/defaulting and intersection remain as previously reviewed. The six collector files are separate research for B, not part of A. No AST summary call remains in either preparation file.
+
+Registered-value parsing constructs ParserContext with no error reporter or use counters, preserving URL data, property ID, None namespaces and whole-substitution AttrTaint. The specified AST is owned until SCC settlement; computation remains after a noncyclic component exits. Parsing is not globally pure: allocation, atom interning, preference reads and attribute/environment queries can occur earlier. This audit does not assume rollback of those effects.
+
+Gecko CssUrl::parse_from_string checks attr taint before URL construction. CssUrl::new_from_string creates an unresolved URL with default owned LoadData. Optional use-counter writes are disabled by this ParserContext. The inspected constructor does not resolve URLs or initiate network loads. URL ToComputedValue clones the specified value. This is a trace of the captured paths, not a claim about all URL consumers.
+
+Image URL/image-set string forms use that taint-checking constructor. Gradient, image-set, cross-fade, image(color), light-dark and Gecko element/icon parsing construct specified structures or atoms. Gecko excludes Servo's paint parser. The inspected -moz-element parser stores an ID atom without a DOM lookup. Contextual image selection and color/light-dark resolution remain in ToComputedValue after SCC settlement. System Color parsing constructs its variant rather than resolving it against current style.
+
+Random key parsing derives property/index identifiers from local declaration context. RandomKey::to_computed_value requests context.random_base_value later. No early random-base evaluation was found; this is not a proof about every transitive calc helper.
+
+Searchfox discovery was followed by exact checkout captures. DISCOVERED-SOURCES.json records nine pairs: seven match; local parser differs only by an inline annotation and local color by the existing InheritFromBodyQuirk spelling. Conclusions follow checkout bodies. These are body pins, not invented revision permalinks. A later fetched computed-length source is separately identified and used only for the zoom trace.
+
+Invalid retains intrinsic COLOR_SCHEME because the invalid-value handler can recompute the registered initial. Inherited invalid values copy the parent's computed value when available. CSS-wide retains its existing copied parent/initial handling. Unknown scans preserve the old head graph mask or propagate live ContextPreparation; neither becomes empty.
+
+Absolute initial lengths still read builder.effective_zoom. The captured cascade resolves custom graph nodes before remaining prioritary properties. Removing an invalid/unused em edge can therefore change readiness; registration independence alone does not prove this harmless. Baseline absolute-length paths may already have related behavior, so no regression is inferred without comparison. The sealed zoom-cases artifact supplies16cases/32snapshots, covering literal/unused/rejected/defaulting modes and fixed/self-dependent font, with Zoom1→2 and physical geometry. It has no conformance oracle.
+
+Serialization matters: captured Value::to_variable_value calls to_css_string directly, whereas captured Servo_GetCustomPropertyValue calls to_resolved_value before serialization. The fetched computed CSSPixelLength resolution divides by style.effective_zoom. A stored length can therefore produce different var() tokens and CSSOM text, and a consuming width can apply zoom again. The observation records custom/width/font CSSOM and bounding geometry separately. No assumed equality substitutes for that trace.
+
+The current446-name regression roster includes two registered-color fallback tests but no explicit image/Zoom assertions. Adjacent-URL numeric attr tests do not by themselves exercise generic registered URL/image admission. URL/image taint and invalid initial-color defaulting remain useful generic-path controls; A104's numeric assertions alone do not cover all generic branches.
+
+Captured CalcNode::Sign calls CalcNodeLeaf::sign_from using unitless_value, so sign(1em) can become Number(1) before the collector. General Product cancellation instead requires canonical values; zero multiplication retains relative units. The [Properties and Values API cycle rule](https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/#dependency-cycles) explicitly covers descriptors with length/length-percentage components, while [Values simplification](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#calc-simplification) permits eager simplification and preserves some zero-unit terms. Those provisions do not alone settle the cycle algorithm's representation boundary or arbitrary numeric self-font semantics.
+
+v2 preserves selected sign(...em) token flags at its boundary while dropping unused fallbacks and invalid whole-value dependencies. Typed-attribute/provider computation may normalize tokens before this boundary; that existing issue is not proven away. The sealed24-case sign observation artifact deliberately has no conformance oracle. A104/B16 were not modified here.
+
+Read-only source review, no native build/browser/index/epoch/canonical changes. No additional concrete v2 code blocker established, but Zoom readiness needs the paired comparison. The Lean law proves local intersection and restriction of a fixed graph, not whole-run cycle preservation as provider/fallback/defaulting outcomes change. No bug-count or coverage increment.
